  pass  EXP: w(1) = w0, -dw/da(1) = wa
  pass  JBP: w(1) = w0, -dw/da(1) = wa
  pass  LOG: w(1) = w0, -dw/da(1) = wa
  pass  BA: w(1) = w0, -dw/da(1) = wa
C1.2 Departure from CPL around a = 1: second derivative d2w/da2 at a = 1 (CPL: 0)
        CPL: 0
        EXP: wa
        JBP: -2*wa
        LOG: wa
        BA: 4*wa
        -> every form equals CPL to first order in (1-a); EXP 'reduces to CPL at first order' (l.271) holds, and so do the other three
C1.3 Early-time limits a -> 0+
        CPL: w0 + wa
        EXP: w0 - wa + E*wa
        JBP: w0
        LOG: oo*wa/Abs(wa)
        BA: w0 + wa
        LOG: w -> -oo for wa < 0 and +oo for wa > 0 (wa*log term); footnote l.285 'the logarithmic term can grow in absolute value' holds
